      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't think the solution should be limited to a specific cause like epilepsy (though I understand your point). There are other reasons that I wouldn't want to revisit a world (it it junk for instance) :-) The Internet seems to be all about \"favorites\" as if we shouldn't be able to rate things unfavorably.\n\nI've long been an advocate of \"tags\" vs \"categorization\". I may mark something as a favorite because I want to explore it later, it isn't a favorite, I haven't seen it. It might be a good example of a bad world that I want to show my friends. Again it isn't a \"favorite\" it should simply be tagged. Then it becomes possible to hide (or show) worlds with particular tags.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-23T21:20:56.243Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I suffer from epilepsy and severe oversensitivity so it would be nice to be able to hide worlds that are known to be triggers. For example I could hide worlds with effects that cannot be disabled or authors who's worlds are known to (unintentionally) trigger a seizure. \n\nHidden worlds should not appear in the worlds tab or search, and have an icon on them in the friends tab while still showing a friend is in there.",
